  "rationale": "All listed candidates are direct matches to basal cell carcinoma (same reported trait/EFO). Among models with comparable validation context (European ancestry; similar MGI-derived training and n=11,322 validation), PGS000452 shows the strongest visible predictive performance: full_model AUROC 0.632 (0.616–0.647) and the highest reported Nagelkerke's pseudo-R² (0.0487), with a strong top 1% vs rest OR (3.61, 2.53–5.15). Close competitors (PGS000454 has essentially identical AUROC 0.632 and pseudo-R² 0.0489; PGS000119 has higher AUROC 0.64 but from a different evaluation setup and without pseudo-R²/Brier reported in the context), so selection is not unequivocal given limited harmonized metrics and some near-ties."
}

{
  "outcome": "DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL",
  "best_model_id": "PGS001263",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "There is a direct-match model for the target trait “atrial flutter” (PGS001263; trait_reported and trait_efo both atrial flutter), whereas the other available candidates are for the combined phenotype “atrial fibrillation and flutter” (including a time-to-event definition for PGS001339), which are not as direct. PGS001263 also provides explicit discrimination metrics in European validation (e.g., PGS-only AUROC 0.61716; full-model AUROC 0.78179 with covariates), while the 2022 portability scores (PGS001841/PGS002050) do not report AUROC/R² here. Limitation: PGS001263 is from UKB with European-selected validation, and the available evidence does not compare head-to-head calibration/utility versus the combined AF/flutter scores or specify whether the intended use case requires flutter-only vs AF+flutter, so the recommendation remains moderately certain rather than high."
}

